      "claim": "L5 gut-wall metabolism records for the corticosteroid class show substantial intestinal first-pass extraction. Budesonide intestinal extraction was 41-64% of the dose (C258). Ketoconazole co-administration increased budesonide AUC 6.5-fold, indicating intestinal CYP3A4 markedly limits systemic exposure (C232). Extensive presystemic elimination via intestinal-wall CYP3A4 was reported (C235, C233). This mechanistic evidence supports presystemic loss for lipophilic corticosteroids and the low direction for the query.",
