  "decision_summary": "Predicted low. L5 gut-wall metabolism records for the corticosteroid class (budesonide intestinal extraction 41-64%, 6.5-fold AUC increase with CYP3A4 inhibition, extensive presystemic elimination) provide mechanistic evidence of presystemic loss. This is consistent with L4 solubility limitations and L3 very low oral exposures for related corticosteroids. High permeability records do not overturn the low direction because first-pass metabolism and solubility dominate. Confidence remains moderate because no direct query F measurement is available."
}

